From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] opengl32: convert an i386 child's GL pointers through its
 window on iOS

opengl32's WoW64 thunks took every 32-bit pointer with ULongToPtr, the
identity on a WoW64 host. On Playport's iOS port an i386 child's address
space is a 4 GiB window at its own host base B (madeira-unix 0049), so its
pointers are B + the 32-bit value, and every guest process shares this unix
side (Playport PLA-162).

make_opengl now writes the WoW64 thunks with the conversion each parameter
needs, and unix_thunks.c is regenerated:

- a pointer to the caller's memory, and the client objects behind HGLRC,
  HPBUFFERARB and GLsync, through the window (wow64_ptr); one handed back
  (a mapped buffer, a created context, pbuffer or sync) back through it
  (wow64_ptr32), a host pointer outside the window reported and NULL;
- GLintptr and GLsizeiptr values, HDC and HENHMETAFILE handles, code
  addresses, EGL objects and glDebugMessageCallback's user data as values;
- a pointer that is an offset into a buffer object when one is bound
  (vertex and attribute arrays, element indices, indirect draws, pixel
  pack and unpack: texture images, glReadPixels, glDrawPixels, glBitmap,
  stipples, colour tables, filters, pixel maps) through the window only
  when the context has no buffer bound to that target, read at the call
  (wow64_ptr_or_offset); glMultiDrawElements' index arrays the same way;
- glGetPointerv's and glGetVertexAttribPointerv's results back through the
  window when they are inside it, as offsets otherwise.

The window base comes from the calling thread's TEB pair (its TEB32's
guest address against where it is), and get_teb64 converts through it.
By hand: return_wow64_string, wow64_get_pixel_formats, the mapped-buffer
pointers and the test for a driver mapping the caller can address go
through the window; thread attach takes the TEB32 it is given as a host
pointer; zero_bits and the debug callback dispatcher are the calling
thread's process's rather than the last process to attach (a WoW64 child
and its x86-64 parent share them); a persistent map for a WoW64 caller,
still unsupported, is logged as an error.

Elsewhere the window base is 0 and the thunks convert as before.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-opengl-i386.md
Offered-upstream: no; the window exists only on the iOS port
---
